title: The Captain
from: Captain Odile Marrow
gist: You told the Captain you're staying aboard the Wren. She's writing to headquarters.
== lines
marrow: You've come about the letter. Go on. I'm listening.   [listen]
marrow > you: Staying. Good. Selfishly, good.   [laugh]
marrow: I'll write to headquarters tonight. Politely. They'll be disappointed, and they'll live.
? choice
* Was it the right answer?   flavour:listen
  marrow: It was your answer. That's the only kind that's right. And yes. I think so.   [nod]
* Tell them thank you, from me.   flavour:share
  marrow: I will. In my best handwriting. Which is still not good.   [laugh]
marrow: You can still change your mind until Sunday. I don't think you will. Carry on, {me}.
